- content_for :title, "How we verify and rank"
- content_for :description, "How StepsFrom measures waterfront properties, what each badge means and how results are ordered."

%section.page-header
  .container
    %h1.page-header__title How we verify and rank
    %p.page-header__lead Our listings are based on measurements, not on what booking sites say.

.container.prose
  %h2 Where the data comes from
  %p
    Properties, coastlines, lakes, beaches and roads come from
    = link_to "OpenStreetMap", "https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright", rel: "noopener"
    (© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL). We do not copy content from booking sites.

  %h2 How we measure
  %p
    We take the property’s building outline (or its position, when no outline is mapped) and measure the shortest
    distance to the shoreline. We then look at the straight line between the two: if a road or railway crosses it,
    the property cannot be “beachfront”, however close it is. Promenades, footpaths and the beach surface are shown
    for information.
  %p
    When a booking site reports a position for the property more than #{@config.fetch(:coordinate_mismatch_m)} m from
    ours, we check it by hand. Every property is reviewed by a person before it is listed, and again whenever a new
    measurement changes its result.

  %h2 What the badges mean
  %dl.badge-legend
    %dt
      %span.badge.badge--direct= t("waterfront.categories.direct")
    %dd
      No road or railway in between, and the water is at most #{@config.fetch(:direct_max_m)} m away — or up to
      #{@config.fetch(:direct_beach_max_m)} m across a mapped beach that starts within
      #{@config.fetch(:beach_adjacent_m)} m of the property.
    %dt
      %span.badge.badge--near= t("waterfront.categories.near")
    %dd The water is at most #{@config.fetch(:near_max_m)} m away, but something (usually a road) lies in between, or it is just beyond the beachfront limits.
    %dt
      %span.badge.badge--walkable= t("waterfront.categories.walkable")
    %dd The water is at most #{@config.fetch(:walkable_max_m)} m away.
  %p Anything further than #{@config.fetch(:walkable_max_m)} m is not listed, even if a booking site calls it beachfront.

  %h2#ranking How results are ordered
  %ul
    %li Without dates: by badge (beachfront first), then by measured distance to the water.
    %li With dates: by the lowest price we have for your dates, then by badge and distance. Properties without a known price come last.
    %li You can switch between the two with “Sort by”.
  %p
    No property can pay to be listed or to rank higher. We earn a commission from booking sites when you book
    through our links (see the
    = succeed ")." do
      = link_to "affiliate disclosure", affiliate_disclosure_path
    Commissions never influence measurements, badges or ordering.

  %h2 Prices
  %p
    Prices come only from official partner programmes of the booking sites. They are cached for a few hours and may
    change; the booking site always shows the final price.
